 "nodes": [
  {
   "id": "root",
   "x": 375,
   "y": 10,
   "w": 760,
   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "Liver enzymes up: HEPATOCELLULAR or CHOLESTATIC pattern?",
   "lines": [
    "enzymes mark DAMAGE or blocked bile flow; they are NOT tests of liver FUNCTION",
    "is it FAILING? albumin ↓, bilirubin ↑, international normalized ratio (INR) ↑: INR is the fastest readout (short half-life)",
    "then ask HOW HIGH, how FAST, WHERE (ethnicity, travel) and WHEN (age, drugs, comorbidities)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_hep",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 156,
   "w": 924,
   "h": 60,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "HEPATOCELLULAR: alanine (ALT) and aspartate (AST) aminotransferase lead",
   "lines": [
    "ALT is the liver-specific one; AST is also in red cells, muscle, brain, gut"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_chol",
   "x": 1009,
   "y": 156,
   "w": 456,
   "h": 60,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "CHOLESTATIC: alkaline phosphatase (ALP) leads",
   "lines": [
    "always read it WITH gamma-glutamyl transferase (GGT)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "t_mild",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 256,
   "w": 456,
   "h": 60,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "MILD: up to 5-10× the upper limit of normal",
   "lines": [
    "which one is HIGHER?"
   ]
  },
